      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nint main() {\n    int n,s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n            scanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i][j]));\n\n    assert(s<n);\n    assert(n<8000);\n    assert(s>0);\n    assert(n>0);\n\n    // Column prefix sums in flat row-major: colPref[i*n + j]\n    std::vector<long long> colPref(n * n);\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        // Compute column prefix sums; each thread handles whole columns.\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for(int j=0;j<n;++j) {\n            long long running = 0;\n            for(int i=0;i<n;++i) {\n                running += matrix[i][j];\n                colPref[i*n + j] = running;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Implicit barrier before the reduction loop.\n\n        // Evaluate every SxS submatrix independently using column prefix sums.\n        // Collapsing both loops increases parallelism and improves load balance,\n        // especially when (n-s+1) is small relative to the number of threads.\n        #pragma omp for collapse(2) schedule(static) reduction(max:mxSum)\n        for(int r=0; r<=n-s; ++r) {\n            for(int c=0; c<=n-s; ++c) {\n                int bottom = r + s - 1;\n                int topMinusOne = r - 1;\n                long long segRight = colPref[bottom*n + (c+s-1)] -\n                                     (topMinusOne >= 0 ? colPref[topMinusOne*n + (c+s-1)] : 0);\n                long long segLeft = 0;\n                if(c > 0) {\n                    int leftCol = c - 1;\n                    segLeft = colPref[bottom*n + leftCol] -\n                              (topMinusOne >= 0 ? colPref[topMinusOne*n + leftCol] : 0);\n                }\n                long long cur = segRight - segLeft;\n                if(cur > mxSum) mxSum = cur;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", (int)mxSum);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using a single OpenMP parallel region for both prefix computation and maximum search, and collapsing the row/column loops to evaluate every SxS submatrix independently via column prefix sums, reduces fork/join overhead and provides finer-grained work sharing. This should improve thread utilization on 4 cores, especially when the number of candidate rows is small.",
  "notes": "The transformation keeps input/output behavior identical. The two original parallel regions are merged into one to avoid repeated fork/join costs. The sliding-window row loop is replaced by a collapsed double loop over all top-left positions; each submatrix sum is computed directly from column prefix sums, removing the sequential dependency and increasing parallelism for small (n-s+1).",
